<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.12.1: Using Coefficients and Constant Terms to Identify Graphs of Linear Equations</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01945</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.12.1: Using Coefficients and Constant Terms to Identify Graphs of Linear Equations</md:title>
    <md:uuid>67b16264-695a-44ff-bac0-2979d94afab1</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
<para>Graphs A, B, and C represent three linear equations:</para>
<para>\(y=2x+4\)</para>
<para>\(y=3-x\)</para>
<para>\(y=3x-2\)</para>
<para>Use the following graph to answer questions 1 – 3.</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Coordinate plane, 3 linear graphs. Line A through negative 2 comma 5 and 3 comma 0. Line B through negative 2 comma 0 and 3 comma 10. Line C through negative 1 comma negative 5 and 4 comma 10."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/57f39f10d61991a2a05c8bdea3c7047ae49b2617"/></media></figure></para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="bed43eb7-4b64-4591-97a3-b897f0c231d3" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0"> &amp;ZeroWidthSpace;

  <!--Q#-->
  &amp;ZeroWidthSpace;
  <exercise data-content-id="a31de486-8285-47f6-a609-39ddfc463ace" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="Graph B" data-solution-options="[&quot;Graph A&quot;, &quot;Graph B&quot;, &quot;Graph C&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which graph corresponds to equation \(y=2x+4\)?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The graph representing \(y=2x+4\) has a slope of 2 and intersects the \(y\)-axis at 4, so it is Graph B. </para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q#2-->
  &amp;ZeroWidthSpace;
  <exercise data-content-id="e11d53d3-0467-49e8-b238-d3076d8bb3b4" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="Graph A" data-solution-options="[&quot;Graph A&quot;, &quot;Graph B&quot;, &quot;Graph C&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which graph corresponds to equation \(y=3-x\)?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The graph representing \(y=3-x\) has a slope of -1 and intersects the \(y\)-axis at 3, so it is Graph A.</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  &amp;ZeroWidthSpace;<!--Q#3-->
  &amp;ZeroWidthSpace;
  <exercise data-content-id="701f4be7-b80f-4b52-bf9f-373ce76324db" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="Graph C" data-solution-options="[&quot;Graph A&quot;, &quot;Graph B&quot;, &quot;Graph C&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which graph corresponds to equation \(y=3x-2\)?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The graph representing \(y=3x-2\) has a slope of 3 and intersects the \(y\)-axis at -2, so it is Graph C.</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
